# fresh_resume_caps: A blob with device info (the guest asked for key 45 first), resumed by a new process in every setup and every pair of setups: the capability check (device_info::check_capabilities, from DeviceCore::check_suspend_device_info) compares the source's host values with the target's, and what the setup changes in them decides whether a migration between differently configured hosts is refused (IncompatibleDevice, 4). Measured on an M3 Max: key 33's bits are 0xbdc in blocks, 0xbdf in map (large user and kernel tasks) and 0xbff in isolate (argument buffers too), and key 42 is 3 in isolate only; a target lacking a bit the source reported refuses (map to blocks, isolate to blocks, isolate to map), the other ways accept. A refused target is left LeavingSuspendEarly: only its registers are read. Host values, so keyed by host.
